1
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:13,179
[Chien-yuan]
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

2
00:00:13,180 --> 00:00:16,390
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

3
00:00:16,391 --> 00:00:19,144
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you... ♪</i>

4
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,354
[lighter clicks]

5
00:00:23,357 --> 00:00:24,733
Something is missing, isn't it?

6
00:00:28,237 --> 00:00:31,405
We need a birthday cake.

7
00:00:31,406 --> 00:00:32,366
[bully] A cake?

8
00:00:32,491 --> 00:00:34,408
- You have one?
- I do.

9
00:00:34,409 --> 00:00:35,827
[laughs]

10
00:00:36,078 --> 00:00:38,413
Here. A red bean cake.

11
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,581
[laughs]

12
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:42,667
Wow...

13
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:44,545
It'll do. [laughs]

14
00:00:44,670 --> 00:00:45,712
Stop eating.

15
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:48,173
Light it.

16
00:00:49,174 --> 00:00:50,259
It's hard to push down.

17
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,555
- What?
- Damn!

18
00:00:54,680 --> 00:00:55,597
- [yells]
- Damn it!

19
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,725
[student groaning]

20
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:01,061
[bully] You're asking for it.

21
00:01:01,186 --> 00:01:02,813
[dramatic music playing]

22
00:01:03,522 --> 00:01:04,606
Teacher.

23
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:20,080
Geez. Where's the lighter?

24
00:01:20,205 --> 00:01:21,247
Here it is.

25
00:01:21,248 --> 00:01:22,541
[tense music playing]

26
00:01:22,666 --> 00:01:24,459
[stove burning]

27
00:01:25,836 --> 00:01:28,130
- [Chien-yuen] Hey.
- [chuckles]

28
00:01:29,548 --> 00:01:31,550
Didn't you say
you want to look good?

29
00:01:32,384 --> 00:01:33,593
How about I give you a perm?

30
00:01:33,594 --> 00:01:35,220
[laughs]

31
00:01:37,180 --> 00:01:40,225
- <i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>
- No! No!

32
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:42,727
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

33
00:01:42,728 --> 00:01:44,395
No!

34
00:01:44,396 --> 00:01:47,815
- No, no, no!
- <i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

35
00:01:47,816 --> 00:01:49,484
[screaming]

36
00:01:51,194 --> 00:01:53,071
- [sizzles]
- [clanks]

37
00:01:53,196 --> 00:01:54,406
[sighs]

38
00:02:07,502 --> 00:02:08,587
[sighs]

39
00:02:11,715 --> 00:02:15,427
[singer] <i>♪ Someday, you can find
Sunshine, sunshine ♪</i>

40
00:02:15,552 --> 00:02:20,265
[singing in Mandarin]

41
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:22,516
<i>♪ Run, run, to hope ♪</i>

42
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,602
<i>♪ Hope, hope, don't go ♪</i>

43
00:02:24,603 --> 00:02:26,647
<i>♪ I believe in you someday ♪</i>

44
00:02:26,772 --> 00:02:28,856
[singing in Mandarin]

45
00:02:28,857 --> 00:02:32,819
<i>♪ Someone just like you
Lights up my dream ♪</i>

46
00:02:32,944 --> 00:02:35,781
[singing in Mandarin]

47
00:02:41,787 --> 00:02:44,665
[piano music playing]

48
00:02:44,790 --> 00:02:46,291
[sighs]

49
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:51,254
[footsteps approaching]

50
00:02:54,466 --> 00:02:55,676
[exhales]

51
00:02:57,969 --> 00:03:00,346
Sorry. Heavy traffic.

52
00:03:00,347 --> 00:03:02,391
[pants]

53
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:05,727
[Chang Ta-chin sighs]

54
00:03:07,646 --> 00:03:10,816
We're here today
to celebrate your graduation.

55
00:03:11,900 --> 00:03:13,567
Congratulations.

56
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:14,653
Thanks, Dad.

57
00:03:14,778 --> 00:03:15,862
Let's eat.

58
00:03:22,202 --> 00:03:23,745
Take this home and look it over.

59
00:03:24,788 --> 00:03:27,207
They're Chang Xin's
financial statements
from the past few years.

60
00:03:27,332 --> 00:03:29,209
You're grown up now.

61
00:03:29,668 --> 00:03:31,753
You should learn more
about the company.

62
00:03:35,257 --> 00:03:36,341
Okay.

63
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:39,928
Dad?

64
00:03:42,431 --> 00:03:44,432
If I go abroad for grad school,

65
00:03:44,433 --> 00:03:45,684
I still want to major
in information engineering.

66
00:03:46,852 --> 00:03:48,769
I think the company
still has a lot of room

67
00:03:48,770 --> 00:03:50,438
to work on digital integration.

68
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:52,315
I want to discuss it with you.

69
00:03:54,359 --> 00:03:56,528
- [smacks lips]
- [clears throat]

70
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:02,743
I think I've told
the two of you before.

71
00:04:02,868 --> 00:04:04,578
As my sons,

72
00:04:04,703 --> 00:04:07,372
you should see things
in a different way from others.

73
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:10,709
I can still help if I major
in information engineering.

74
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:11,710
How?

75
00:04:12,753 --> 00:04:14,880
I want you to learn
to manage the company,

76
00:04:15,005 --> 00:04:16,381
not to be an engineer.

77
00:04:16,506 --> 00:04:18,008
Tell me.

78
00:04:18,258 --> 00:04:20,718
Do you know how many
employees or shareholders

79
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:22,762
we have to take care of
in Chang Xin?

80
00:04:22,763 --> 00:04:23,929
Dad...

81
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:26,057
Do you know how much
the annual output value

82
00:04:26,308 --> 00:04:27,893
of these pork knuckles
contributes to our company?

83
00:04:28,018 --> 00:04:30,270
How to make them?
What's their breed?

84
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:32,355
Where are they from?
How to negotiate the price?

85
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,024
You can't even be punctual.

86
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:35,609
What do you want
to talk to me about?

87
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:39,446
Listen to me. How old am I?

88
00:04:39,571 --> 00:04:43,825
How much time do I have left
to help you and your brother?

89
00:04:48,413 --> 00:04:50,790
If you don't know what to do,
just follow my orders.

90
00:04:50,791 --> 00:04:52,750
From now until Father's Day,

91
00:04:52,751 --> 00:04:55,420
you'll be in charge
of one brand each.

92
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:56,754
I'll be in charge of one brand?

93
00:04:56,755 --> 00:04:58,506
That's right.

94
00:04:58,507 --> 00:05:00,758
Hsiu-wen will manage
Jin Lai Xuan.

95
00:05:00,759 --> 00:05:03,469
Chien-yuen,
you're familiar with Chang Xin.

96
00:05:03,470 --> 00:05:04,929
I'll give you a chance.

97
00:05:04,930 --> 00:05:07,349
Prove yourself.
Don't let me down.

98
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,434
Okay.

99
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:11,603
No problem.

100
00:05:12,437 --> 00:05:14,940
As for you, you used to be
an intern at Mianzi.

101
00:05:15,065 --> 00:05:16,732
Yeah.

102
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:18,944
You'll be in charge
of the Father's Day event.

103
00:05:19,611 --> 00:05:22,280
I'll send people to help you.
Learn from them, okay?

104
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:24,407
[suspenseful music playing]

105
00:05:27,452 --> 00:05:28,536
[chuckles]

106
00:05:28,537 --> 00:05:29,955
[yelps]

107
00:05:34,626 --> 00:05:36,086
[yells, grunts]

108
00:05:36,962 --> 00:05:38,964
[grunting]

109
00:05:40,006 --> 00:05:42,008
[panting]

110
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:50,100
[breathes deeply]

111
00:05:51,935 --> 00:05:53,019
[exhales]

112
00:05:54,604 --> 00:05:55,813
[dramatic music playing]

113
00:05:55,814 --> 00:05:56,982
[gasps]

114
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:59,943
[panting and grunting]

115
00:06:12,581 --> 00:06:14,498
[screaming]

116
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:15,667
Shit!

117
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:22,340
[tense music playing]

118
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,009
[grunting and panting continues]

119
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:28,889
[screams]

120
00:06:29,556 --> 00:06:31,391
Come on! Why?

121
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:34,603
[yells]

122
00:06:37,647 --> 00:06:38,607
Damn!

123
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:40,942
[gasping breath]

124
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,737
[panting]

125
00:06:54,039 --> 00:06:55,706
[Yi-hsuan]
<i>A chef who's afraid of fire.</i>

126
00:06:55,707 --> 00:06:58,626
I've never heard of anything
more absurd.

127
00:06:58,627 --> 00:07:01,128
I don't know why you hired her.

128
00:07:01,129 --> 00:07:03,214
You can't make a silk purse
out of a sow's ear.

129
00:07:10,889 --> 00:07:12,556
I don't know
why you're afraid of fire.

130
00:07:12,557 --> 00:07:13,934
And I don't care,
and I don't want to hear it.

131
00:07:15,894 --> 00:07:18,103
<i>We need consistent flavors.</i>

132
00:07:18,104 --> 00:07:19,481
If you can't do it,
just get lost.

133
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:24,903
[dramatic music playing]

134
00:07:32,827 --> 00:07:35,830
[upbeat jazz music playing]

135
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:43,796
The noodles with peppercorn
chili oil you're eating now

136
00:07:43,797 --> 00:07:45,589
are our most stable product
on the market

137
00:07:45,590 --> 00:07:47,591
with the highest
repeat purchase rate.

138
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:50,261
This is also
my personal favorite.

139
00:07:50,512 --> 00:07:52,263
Maybe we'll make this
our featured dish.

140
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:55,809
Maybe, but I think
what matters now

141
00:07:55,934 --> 00:07:57,644
is not to decide
on our feature dish.

142
00:07:57,769 --> 00:08:00,854
Our target group of customers
is the nine-to-fivers.

143
00:08:00,855 --> 00:08:01,939
They're here for a quick meal.

144
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:03,233
Why don't they go

145
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:04,817
to a higher-end restaurant
to celebrate?

146
00:08:04,818 --> 00:08:06,694
How do we attract them
to come here?

147
00:08:06,695 --> 00:08:07,946
I think that's what matters.

148
00:08:08,071 --> 00:08:10,156
In fact, we offered
some discounts before,

149
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:12,617
- but didn't attract
many customers.
- Hmm.

150
00:08:13,868 --> 00:08:15,704
- [Hsiu-wen] Hello.
- Hi.

151
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,455
Hey.

152
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:19,665
- Why are you here?
- Here's what you asked for.

153
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:20,959
I've brought them to you.

154
00:08:21,084 --> 00:08:22,669
We've got work to do.
We'll leave you alone.

155
00:08:22,794 --> 00:08:25,547
Yeah. Take your time.

156
00:08:25,964 --> 00:08:27,298
[Hsiu-wen] New flavors?

157
00:08:27,549 --> 00:08:30,676
No. We're deciding
on our featured dish.

158
00:08:30,677 --> 00:08:31,803
Want to have a taste?

159
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:32,971
- Okay.
- [chuckles]

160
00:08:36,808 --> 00:08:38,059
Thanks.

161
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:42,981
Does it feel a bit pathetic
to eat noodles on Father's Day?

162
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:46,191
Tastes good. Actually,
the flavor isn't the issue.

163
00:08:46,192 --> 00:08:49,236
Your target audience
should be those

164
00:08:49,237 --> 00:08:50,655
who don't normally
celebrate Father's Day,

165
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:52,657
not those who already
celebrate it.

166
00:08:54,242 --> 00:08:56,535
Those who normally
don't celebrate Father's Day?

167
00:08:56,536 --> 00:08:57,370
Yep.

168
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:05,128
Think of some plans
to attract those people.

169
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:16,055
Sorry.
These are your chopsticks.

170
00:09:16,056 --> 00:09:17,724
It's okay. I don't mind.

171
00:09:17,849 --> 00:09:19,184
My mind was elsewhere. Sorry.

172
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:20,852
Yeah, thanks.

173
00:09:22,771 --> 00:09:25,690
[engines revving]

174
00:09:34,032 --> 00:09:35,033
[Chien-yuan] Hey.

175
00:09:39,788 --> 00:09:41,246
How are things?

176
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:42,832
Happy selling noodles?

177
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,211
Yeah, of course.

178
00:09:48,379 --> 00:09:51,216
Did Hsiu-wen go to help you?

179
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:54,301
Yeah.

180
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,887
What's wrong?

181
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:58,722
I want you
to stay away from her.

182
00:09:58,723 --> 00:09:59,641
[scoffs]

183
00:10:01,101 --> 00:10:03,103
Damn.
Don't you want to study abroad?

184
00:10:03,228 --> 00:10:04,728
Go now.

185
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:06,606
Don't fall in love with her.

186
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:09,109
Listen. You have no chance.

187
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:11,986
She won't love
a young boy like you.

188
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,573
She won't love
a killer like you.

189
00:10:15,698 --> 00:10:17,909
[tense music playing]

190
00:10:23,248 --> 00:10:26,251
Don't say what you don't know.

191
00:10:27,335 --> 00:10:29,086
Shut your trap!

192
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:30,171
Hear me?

193
00:10:34,092 --> 00:10:35,844
[elevator bell dings]

194
00:10:44,811 --> 00:10:46,896
[music continues]

195
00:10:54,863 --> 00:10:57,781
- [camera clicks]
- [photographer]
Alright, look here!

196
00:10:57,782 --> 00:10:59,950
Nice.
Keep it that way.

197
00:10:59,951 --> 00:11:02,286
Is it confirmed that
he's the successor to Chang Xin?

198
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:04,288
Doesn't he have a brother?

199
00:11:04,289 --> 00:11:06,791
I can't give you an answer.

200
00:11:06,916 --> 00:11:10,169
But I've heard his brother
is smart, not ambitious.

201
00:11:10,170 --> 00:11:12,004
<i>All he wants to do
is work in tech development.</i>

202
00:11:12,005 --> 00:11:14,840
<i>He's not interested
in managing a company.</i>

203
00:11:14,841 --> 00:11:17,135
<i>It's said that
the chairman got furious</i>

204
00:11:17,260 --> 00:11:18,636
<i>and sent him
to a small noodle diner</i>

205
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,346
<i>to handle
the Father's Day event.</i>

206
00:11:21,264 --> 00:11:25,476
<i>His dad wanted him to know that
he's inexperienced and naïve.</i>

207
00:11:25,727 --> 00:11:28,146
On the other hand,
Chien-yuen is very ambitious.

208
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:32,191
He's been learning everything
from his dad, very experienced.

209
00:11:32,192 --> 00:11:33,651
My money's on him.

210
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:37,237
Hey, why don't you try
to place your elbow on the rail?

211
00:11:37,238 --> 00:11:38,197
Like this?

212
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:39,490
Cool!

213
00:11:39,741 --> 00:11:41,868
The headline will be
"Successor to a Dining Empire".

214
00:11:41,993 --> 00:11:43,661
- Is that okay?
- Yeah, sure.

215
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:45,413
- Okay, not a problem.
- [man] Thank you so much.

216
00:11:50,335 --> 00:11:51,794
[Chien-wu] You want some too?

217
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:53,837
But it's too salty.

218
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:55,215
I can't give you any.

219
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:00,803
[whimpers]

220
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:04,807
[energetic music playing]

221
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:09,854
Got an idea.

222
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:13,524
Thank you.

223
00:12:16,444 --> 00:12:18,154
- Chien-yuen!
- Hey!

224
00:12:19,489 --> 00:12:21,491
I've got you an expert.

225
00:12:21,741 --> 00:12:23,408
Lin Shih-ching, a sommelier

226
00:12:23,409 --> 00:12:26,246
who won the RVF
Blind Tasting Championship.

227
00:12:26,371 --> 00:12:29,164
He hand-picks all the wines
our family distributes.

228
00:12:29,165 --> 00:12:31,041
[Shih-ching]
Although it's a wine pairing
for the Father's Day menu,

229
00:12:31,042 --> 00:12:33,961
I'd like to start with
the Lolea No.4 sparkling wine.

230
00:12:33,962 --> 00:12:36,088
With its bubbles blended
with the refreshing aromas

231
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:37,923
of lemon juice and cardamom,

232
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,385
it's perfect for targeting
the female family members.

233
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:43,763
Not bad.

234
00:12:44,472 --> 00:12:45,973
We're all fathers!
To create a sense

235
00:12:45,974 --> 00:12:47,725
of companionship
in the loneliness economy,

236
00:12:47,850 --> 00:12:49,142
Father's Day for fur babies.

237
00:12:49,143 --> 00:12:51,895
All customers
who order a Father's Day combo

238
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:53,981
and show us a photo
with their fur babies

239
00:12:53,982 --> 00:12:56,025
will receive a free gift,

240
00:12:57,277 --> 00:12:59,111
human-grade freeze-dried meat.

241
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:01,906
Whatever dad eats,
his fur baby eats too.

242
00:13:04,534 --> 00:13:08,203
Do ferrets or chameleons
count as fur babies?

243
00:13:08,204 --> 00:13:09,372
[light gasps]

244
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:12,083
If you prefer a stronger flavor,

245
00:13:12,208 --> 00:13:13,751
we have this bottle of whiskey

246
00:13:13,876 --> 00:13:16,212
to go with the diverse tastes
of Taiwanese cuisine,

247
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:17,797
especially seafood.

248
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:19,966
A whiskey to go with seafood?

249
00:13:21,050 --> 00:13:23,303
One of my friends has a chicken.
Does that count?

250
00:13:23,428 --> 00:13:24,595
Yeah, does that count?

251
00:13:24,846 --> 00:13:27,974
- A chicken...
- Yeah, my friend has a musk pig.

252
00:13:28,099 --> 00:13:29,474
So I think...

253
00:13:29,475 --> 00:13:31,102
But it doesn't feel right
to feed pork to a pig.

254
00:13:31,227 --> 00:13:32,270
[sighs]

255
00:13:32,395 --> 00:13:34,104
Actually,
your idea is pretty good.

256
00:13:34,105 --> 00:13:35,440
But let's limit
our eligible pets

257
00:13:35,565 --> 00:13:37,150
to the most common
cats and dogs.

258
00:13:37,275 --> 00:13:38,317
That will give us
a more specific direction

259
00:13:38,318 --> 00:13:39,819
for our preparation.

260
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,153
Where do the gifts come from?

261
00:13:41,154 --> 00:13:43,114
